    "id": "q_sports_20260108_008_e665850f",
    "title": "Which of these wrestlers will Gunther face at a major WWE pay-per-view event in 2026?",
    "question_type": "mcq",
    "options": [
      "Cody Rhodes"
    ],
    "background": "No background available.",
    "resolution_criteria": "Gunther must have a one-on-one match against one of the listed wrestlers at a major WWE PPV in 2026.",
    "outcome": "Cody Rhodes",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nThe outcome of Cody Rhodes facing Gunther at a major WWE pay-per-view in 2026 was largely driven by a storyline pivot that occurred in late 2025. After initially being slated for a match against Roman Reigns or Randy Orton, Cody Rhodes lost his Undisputed WWE Championship to Drew McIntyre due to interference from Jacob Fatu. Stripped of his championship, Cody's path shifted towards the World Heavyweight Championship held by Gunther. This led to a deeply personal rivalry, with Gunther critiquing Cody's legacy, culminating in a booked 2026 PPV match.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- Early 2025: Rumors suggest Cody Rhodes will face Roman Reigns or Randy Orton at WrestleMania 42. [art_sports_20260316_013_481909bb]\n- Late 2025: Cody Rhodes loses the Undisputed WWE Championship to Drew McIntyre following interference by Jacob Fatu. [art_sports_20260316_015_b99e715a]\n- Late 2025/Early 2026: Without the WWE Championship, Cody pivots his attention to the World Heavyweight Champion, Gunther. [art_sports_20260310_004_a87d0eb8]\n- March 2026: Gunther continuously attacks Cody's work ethic and legacy in promos on Raw and SmackDown, escalating the feud. [art_sports_20260313_014_53427dbb]\n- March 2026: Match between Gunther and Cody Rhodes is heavily teased and rumored as a \"Career Ending Match\" for WrestleMania 42. [art_sports_20260226_017_950be9e6]\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause of this storyline was WWE's creative decision to have Cody Rhodes lose his Undisputed WWE Championship. This loss was triggered by Jacob Fatu's interference, allowing Drew McIntyre to win the title. [art_sports_20260316_015_b99e715a] As an intermediate mechanism, this loss forced Cody to find a new path to the top of the card, leading him to target the other major title: Gunther's World Heavyweight Championship. The proximate triggers were the escalating promos where Gunther attacked Cody's work ethic [art_sports_20260310_004_a87d0eb8], creating a personal rivalry that necessitated a major pay-per-view payoff, resulting in their scheduled 2026 match.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nThe primary countervailing factors were the strong pre-existing storylines and fan expectations for Cody Rhodes to face either Roman Reigns in a sequel match or his former mentor Randy Orton for the WWE Championship. Additionally, Cody could have logically pursued a revenge storyline directly against Jacob Fatu. However, these paths were overwhelmed by WWE's desire to elevate the World Heavyweight Championship picture and create a fresh, high-stakes dynamic by pitting the resilient Cody against the dominant ring general, Gunther.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: Cody Rhodes loses WWE Championship to Drew McIntyre\n  - Date: Late 2025\n  - Why it matters causally: Stripped Cody of his title, forcing him to seek a new championship path.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_sports_20260316_015_b99e715a]\n- E2: Jacob Fatu interferes in championship match\n  - Date: Late 2025\n  - Why it matters causally: The direct mechanism that caused Cody's title loss.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_sports_20260316_015_b99e715a]\n- E3: Gunther insults Cody's work ethic\n  - Date: March 2026\n  - Why it matters causally: Escalated the sporting contest into a deeply personal feud requiring a major PPV resolution.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_sports_20260310_004_a87d0eb8]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Cody loses to McIntyre via Fatu | [art_sports_20260316_015_b99e715a] | 2025 | 0.8 | Sets up the pivot. |\n| Gunther critiques Cody's work ethic | [art_sports_20260310_004_a87d0eb8] | Mar 2026 | 0.9 | Builds the feud. |\n| Gunther vs Cody at WM42 teased | [art_sports_20260226_017_950be9e6] | Feb/Mar 2026 | 0.9 | Final outcome confirmation. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThere is some uncertainty regarding the exact PPV (WrestleMania vs Crown Jewel vs SummerSlam) where the match will take place, though rumors strongly point to WrestleMania 42. An alternative path would have seen Cody regain the WWE Championship from McIntyre, or Roman Reigns challenging Gunther instead.\n",
